 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Esoteric Art — Innate Technique (6th level)</em></p><p>At 6th level, you have improved your technique. You can now manipulate your painting as a bonus action and gain the following improvements and options:<br />\n<strong>Ink Shikigami</strong>. You can summon new types of shikigami:<br />\n<a href=\"https://5e.tools/bestiary/young-winter-wolf-tftyp.html\">Greater Ink Wolf</a> (2 CE)<br />\n<a href=\"https://5e.tools/bestiary/giant-eagle-mm.html\">Ink Crow</a> (3 CE)<br />\n<strong>Exit Shift</strong>. You cause the location of the <em>Exit Painting</em> to a new random accessible location in the subspace.<br />\n<strong>Difficult Terrain</strong>. You can now create a 30 ft radius area of difficult terrain anywhere within your painting.<br />\n<strong>Structure Generation</strong>. Each 5 ft by 5 ft section of a structure you create now has hit points equal to 10 x your proficiency bonus.<br />\n<strong>Trap Creation</strong>. Your traps now deal an additional 2 damage dice. This increases to an additional 4 damage dice at 11th level.<br />\n<strong>Ink Wave</strong>. As an action for 2 cursed energy, you create a 30 ft cone originating from you or an <em>Ink Shikigami</em>. A creature within the cone must make a Constitution saving throw, taking your proficiency bonus in d6s of necrotic damage and be blinded until the end of their next turn on a failed save. (This can also be used outside your subspace)<br />\n<strong>Larger Frames</strong>. You can now use <em>Cursed Painting</em> on Large or smaller creatures. This increases to Huge at 11th level.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
